# Faceted Flight: 10th Anniversary Edition: environment template.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # .env is gitignored; .env.example is not
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_ to browser code. Anything with that
# prefix is PUBLIC: it ends up inlined as a string in the built bundle. Never put
# a secret in this file or in .env.


# ── Where the game finds its content ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# The game loads models, terrain maps, music and the cockpit font at runtime, from
# this base URL. None of that is in git. The default, "/", means "serve it from
# Vite's public/ directory", which is where `pnpm content:pull` unpacks the open
# content pack. See docs/assets.md.
#
# Unset or blank is a hard failure at boot that names this variable, not a
# fallback, so a missing setting is a readable error rather than a black screen.
#
# Point it at your own static host only if you host a copy of the content pack
# yourself. No trailing slash needed, though one is tolerated.
VITE_ASSET_BASE_URL=/


# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Emit browsable source maps from `pnpm build`. Off by default: the build writes
# hidden source maps without publishing a sourceMappingURL.
# SOURCEMAP=1

# Which feature set a build ships. A local build is the "preview" channel, which
# shows everything including the aircraft variants and the glider. Set this to
# "release" to build what the live site's production channel ships.
# FF2_CHANNEL=release


# ── Tooling only: not read by the game ───────────────────────────────────
#
# These are read by scripts under tools/, not by Vite. They need no VITE_ prefix
# and must never acquire one.

# OPTIONAL, and only for regenerating content. The generated trees in content/
# and src/generated/ were extracted from the original 2016 Unity project, which is
# not distributed. You do not need it: the committed output is checked against
# its recorded hashes by `pnpm extract:check`, with no Unity project present. If
# you own a copy of the 2016 game's project and want to re-run the extractors,
# set this to its root folder. The tools only ever READ from it.
# FF2_LEGACY=/path/to/the/unity/project

# OPTIONAL, with FF2_LEGACY: the folder holding the two read-only reference
# projects some porting notes compare against. If unset it is derived from
# FF2_LEGACY (three levels up). Nothing in the game or its tests needs it.
# FF2_REF=/path/to/the/reference/projects

# Where tools/assets/check-assets-present.mjs looks for an unpacked content tree.
# Manifest paths are relative to it. Defaults to public.
# ASSET_DIR=public
